WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.300
Two bearings aren’t the only way to get a fix.

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:08.250
A bearing and a radar range on the same object make an excellent one.

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:13.575
The line and the circle cross at a right angle, and you only need one landmark.

4
00:00:13.825 --> 00:00:18.650
Radar ranges to two different objects give two circles, and they cross.

5
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.150
A range line, plus a bearing on something else, works very well.

6
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:29.100
A GPS fix is marked with a small triangle, so you can tell it from a visual fix.

7
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:33.575
And whatever method you use, cross-check it against another source.

8
00:00:33.825 --> 00:00:36.100
What’s the easiest check you have?

9
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.825
The depth sounder.

10
00:00:39.075 --> 00:00:43.800
If the fix says twenty feet and the sounder says six, believe the sounder.

11
00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:45.950
That’s lesson six.

12
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.700
Draw bearings back from the object.

13
00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:51.350
Cross them near ninety degrees.

14
00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.975
A big cocked hat means a mistake.

15
00:00:54.225 --> 00:00:56.525
Next time: dead reckoning.
